'''Tumeken's heka''' was a proposed powered wand requiring 85 [[Magic]] to equip. It belonged to [[Tumeken]], the head of the [[Menaphite Pantheon]], and was given to Pharaoh [[Osmumten]] by [[Elidinis]] after his sacrifice that ended the [[Kharidian–Zarosian War]]. It was only available from the [[Supplies (unrestricted world)|supplies]] table in an [[unrestricted world]] as a test item for players, and was one of the proposed rewards for the [[Tombs of Amascut]] raid.

Although Tumeken's heka passed [[Poll:Tombs of Amascut Rewards|its poll]], it was proposed to be replaced by the [[Shadow of Tumeken]] in a [[Update:Tombs of Amascut: Reward Changes|poll blog]] two months later, due to continued player feedback on the desire for a magic weapon that would "redefine Magic as a combat style just as the Scythe [of Vitur] and Twisted Bow did." It was then polled in the [[Poll:Tombs of Amascut Reward Changes|Tombs of Amascut Reward Changes]] [[poll]] with the caveat that the heka would be replaced with the Shadow of Tumeken if it passed the poll; this came to pass with 90.9% support.

In order to use the wand's magic spell, it must be charged with [[soul rune|soul]] and [[chaos rune]]s, holding up to 20,000 charges when fully charged. Each cast requires 1 soul rune and 3 chaos runes, costing {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Soul rune|1}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune|3}}|c}} per cast. The total cost to fully charge the wand with 20,000 soul and 60,000 chaos runes is {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Soul rune|20000}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune|60000}}|c}}. Players can uncharge the wand whenever and wherever they choose, getting all of their runes back.

