==Spell mechanics==
[[File:Tumeken's heka.gif|thumb|280px|A player using Tumeken's heka's built in spell.]]
Like [[powered staves]], Tumeken's heka has a built-in magic spell that can be used regardless of the [[spellbook]] the player is using and cannot be used to autocast any other combat spells.

The heka's spell is an attack in which players will attack the target with three fast attacks, followed by a charged attack that deals significantly more damage (alongside a secondary effect dependent on the player's active [[spellbook]]), albeit with a longer delay after the attack. The first three fast attacks have an attack speed of two [[ticks]] (1.2 seconds), with the fourth charged attack having an attack speed of four [[ticks]] (2.4 seconds).

The spell '''cannot''' be used against other players in the [[Wilderness]]. The only way that the spell can be used against other players is during the [[Castle Wars]], [[Soul Wars]] and [[TzHaar Fight Pit]] [[minigame]]s, as well as the [[Clan Wars]] minigame if the clan leaders enable it.

===Charged attack mechanics===
The heka's charged attack also carries with it a secondary effect that is dependent on the player's active [[spellbook]]:

{| class="wikitable align-center-1" style="text-align:left; width:550px;"
! colspan="2" |Spellbook
!Effect
|-
|{{plinkt|Standard spellbook}}
|The heka's charged attack will have its damage increased by 10%.
|-
|{{plinkt|Ancient Magicks|pic=Ancient spellbook}}
|The heka's charged attack will strike in a 3x3 Area of Effect around its primary target.
|-
|{{plinkt|Lunar spellbook}}
|The heka's attack range is increased to 7 squares for all attacks, and the charged attack will heal up to five allies along the path of the spell by 5% of the caster's current Magic level, rounded down.
|-
|{{plinkt|Arceuus spellbook}}
|At the cost of three [[prayer points]], the heka's charged attack will drain 5% of the target's Magic level (capped at 20%), and boost the caster's Magic level by 50% of the drained levels from the target, up to a 15% increase of the caster's Magic level.
|}

===Maximum hit===
The [[Maximum Magic hit|maximum hit]] dealt by Tumeken's heka is dependent on the player's current [[Magic]] level; the formula for the heka's fast and charged attacks are as follows. Note that any [[magic damage]] bonuses are applied after the base max hit is calculated.

<math>\begin{align}
Fast &= \frac{Magic}{6} + 1\\
Charged &= \frac{Magic - 25}{2}\\
\end{align}</math>

